collins (0.1.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Collins is now published to ppa:episode6/stable, for Ubuntu 24.04 (noble)
    and 26.04 (resolute).
  * Install alongside agent-session-manager instead of colliding with it: the
    action icons move out of the shared hicolor theme into
    /usr/share/collins/icons, which both packages claimed copies of
    (agent-claude-symbolic.svg and tab-close-symbolic.svg).
  * Require libadwaita 1.5 and GTK 4.10 explicitly, so a distribution too old
    to run Collins refuses the package instead of installing it and failing at
    launch.
  * libspelling is optional now (Depends -> Recommends): without it the
    prompt composer is a plain text box instead of refusing to launch the
    app.
  * Every keyboard shortcut is rebindable from a Keyboard Bindings dialog in
    the sidebar menu; Ctrl+K is the quick switcher, Ctrl+Shift+K clears the
    terminal panel, and Ctrl+Shift+F no longer opens the sidebar search.
  * Close can hide the window and keep every session running; the status
    icon, a notification, or relaunching brings it back.
  * Collins is on PyPI as plain "collins", and the sidebar menu offers the
    Ubuntu PPA to an install that didn't come from it.
  * Session tools: start_session takes a model, and a spawned sibling
    inherits the caller's model and permission mode.
  * Generate Icon picks its model per run; the model list is cached for a
    day and across restarts, with a Refresh row in Preferences, and the
    pickers group it by family.
  * The project row's menu pulls its branch; the composer opens on typing by
    default and never loses a draft; its spell-check menu aims at the word
    you clicked.
  * PR pages open wider when the gutter is free, render changed images as
    images, and follow running checks with free conditional requests instead
    of waiting for the next minute.
  * Ctrl+click finishes a wrapped link from the transcript when the screen
    can't.
  * Preferences regrouped into ten groups; notifications withdraw themselves
    when what they say stops being true.
  * Fixes: archiving clears a session's notification and unread count; the
    status icon's menu no longer draws "Quit" on a separator; a click in the
    gutter beside a width-limited terminal focuses it and clears unread.

 -- Geoff Hackett <ghackett@episode6.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 07:21:01 -0400

